{
  "risk_synthesis": "Two of the three context fields are genuine risk multipliers under the rules: (1) Weather — heavy rain on wet asphalt directly degrades traction and visibility, a clear risk multiplier; (2) Schedule pressure — running 20 minutes behind schedule is an explicit risk factor per the rules. Cargo (liquids/chemical tanker) is also a risk multiplier because it is hazardous and liquid, meaning any loss of control or hard braking could cause a spill or shift. All three fields independently qualify as risk multipliers, so the combined operational context strongly supports moving away from the baseline. All three fields independently qualify as risk multipliers, so the heavy rain, hazardous liquid cargo, and schedule pressure together create a compounded risk profile that justifies escalation.",
